---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { SITE_TITLE } from "../consts";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`Privacy · ${SITE_TITLE}`}
  description="Privacy notice for Papermerge News."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy Notice</h1>

    <p>
      This notice covers the Papermerge News site
      (<strong>www.papermerge.blog</strong>) only. The Papermerge application
      (<code>app.papermerge.com</code>) and the main website
      (<code>papermerge.com</code>) have their own privacy policies.
    </p>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>
      Eugen Ciur, Trusetaler Straße 90, 12687 Berlin, Germany<br />
      E-mail: <a href="mailto:eugen@papermerge.com">eugen@papermerge.com</a>
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a set of static files hosted on <strong>GitHub Pages</strong>,
      a service of GitHub, Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA
      94107, USA. When you open a page, your browser necessarily transmits your
      IP address and request metadata (requested URL, timestamp, referrer, user
      agent) to GitHub, which may process this data in server logs to deliver the
      content and protect the service against attacks.
    </p>
    <p>
      Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in operating a secure,
      functioning website). This processing involves a transfer to the USA;
      GitHub provides appropriate safeguards through EU Standard Contractual
      Clauses. See GitHub's
      <a
        href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">privacy statement</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>No cookies, no tracking</h2>
    <p>
      This site sets no cookies and uses no analytics, tracking, advertising, or
      third-party embeds. It loads no external fonts or scripts. There are no
      contact forms or user accounts. The RSS feed is a static file; subscribing
      happens in your feed reader and is not recorded here.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of
      processing, and objection, and the right to lodge a complaint with a
      supervisory authority — for Berlin, the
      <a
        href="https://www.datenschutz-berlin.de/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >Berliner Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit</a
      >.
    </p>
  </article>

  <p class="back-link"><a href="/">&larr; Back to News</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
